From 3419edeb1ee3f69c4a12c4215aba032d3bee4c57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:02:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 80/80] MAS local: tighten the lean safe shutdown state and
 logging

- Count the forced-exit state as shutting down: a close request in the
  seconds before QEMU quits (taskkill without /f posts WM_CLOSE to the
  hidden window) no longer falls through to the upstream close path,
  which takes the snapshot lock or runs "adb shell stop".
- The adb callbacks run on the AdbInterface looper and can complete
  after the window is torn down; they now post to it only while it is
  alive, checked under a lock that the destructor takes.
- Do not ask whether to save a quick-boot snapshot and do not save one:
  the guest is powering off, and a snapshot of it shutting down would
  resume the shutdown on the next quick boot. The manager and AUTO-MAS
  boot with -no-snapshot, so only instances started by hand are
  affected.
- Log through dinfo/dwarning. LOG() from this file does not reach the
  emulator log, so the timeout and failure paths left no trace.

Change-Id: Iabc5ed7c4c92fa17d07d12361b124a956cef201c
---
 .../android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp    | 57 ++++++++++++++-----
 .../src/android/skin/qt/tool-window.cpp       | 13 +++--
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp b/android/android-ui/modules/aemu-ui-qt/src/android/skin/qt/emulator-qt-window.cpp
